/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - For a cycle, follow every small heat transfer δQ across the boundary of the system.
   - δQ is the small heat transfer in kJ, positive into the system and negative out of it; T is the boundary temperature in kelvin at which that heat crosses; ∮ means the sum around one complete cycle.
   - For a cycle with a few separate heat transfers, use Σ Qi/Ti ≤ 0 with the same sign rule.
   - Suppose a cycle gave a positive total, ∮δQ/T > 0.
   - The argument works for any T₀ > 0.
   - For a cycle that exchanges heat with one reservoir only, at T₀, the integral is Qin/T₀ − Qout/T₀ = (Qin − Qout)/T₀ = W/T₀.
*/
